' 25 The priority queue: levels of records and lanes of waiters.
'
' Source of Figure N11.10 in ../design.md (section N11.10). The figure restates
' PQ-OFFER and PQ-RECEIVE of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/disciplines/priority_queue.rs
' (decision 38). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. A send with priority p goes to the level p, and a send without a
'      priority goes to the unprioritized level, which comes last (F6).
'   2. A record that is not at the FIFO place of the head of its level is
'      stored (decision 43 for a re-entered record).
'   3. Otherwise the send offers the record to the head of the lane Level(p)
'      and to the head of the lane Any, the older head first. A refusal moves
'      on to the other head.
'   4. A receive with priority p waits in the lane Level(p), and a receive
'      without a priority waits in the lane Any. It binds the first level head
'      that its lane sees and checks its guard once, on that head.
'   5. After each plan the queue settles: the oldest fireable lane head fires
'      first (readiness review S4).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 25-priority-queue-lanes.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 25-priority-queue-lanes
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The priority queue (P5b): levels of records and lanes of waiters

start
:open_plan: the settle before the plan, on the one
fire count of the transaction (decision 49); <<$rrs_agent>>
split
  partition "send (PQ-OFFER)" {
    :ℓ ← the level of priority = p, or the unprioritized
    level, which comes after every priority level (F6); <<$rrs_agent>>
    if (the record is at the FIFO place of the head of level ℓ?) then (yes)
      :offer to the heads of the lanes Level(ℓ) and Any,
      the older head first (decision 38); <<$rrs_agent>>
      if (a head binds and admits the datum?) then (yes)
        :fire that head; <<$rrs_effect>>
      else (no: each head refused)
        :store the record in level ℓ; <<$rrs_storage>>
      endif
    else (no)
      :store the record at its FIFO place in level ℓ; <<$rrs_storage>>
    endif
  }
split again
  partition "receive (PQ-RECEIVE)" {
    :L ← the lane Level(p), or the lane Any
    when the receive has no priority; <<$rrs_agent>>
    if (the waiter is at the head of its lane L?) then (yes)
      :h ← the first level head that L sees
      whose payload the pattern binds; <<$rrs_agent>>
      if (a head h was found and the guard admits it?) then (yes)
        :fire on h; a peek of a non-persistent h
        stores h again at its order (Rule E); <<$rrs_effect>>
      else (no)
        :park the waiter in lane L
        (the guard is checked once); <<$rrs_storage>>
      endif
    else (no)
      :park the waiter at its place in lane L; <<$rrs_storage>>
    endif
  }
end split
:the settle after the plan fires the oldest
fireable lane head first (readiness review S4); <<$rrs_flow>>
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_agent>    | a choice of the plan |
|<$rrs_effect>   | a staged fire |
|<$rrs_storage>  | a stored record or a parked waiter |
|<$rrs_flow>     | the settle of exposed pairs |
endlegend
@enduml
